At 07:13 PM 11/29/02 -0500, Craig wrote:
> >> But the policy is not open to amendment at this point
>
> >For this very reason, I will vote against it, even though I agree with
> >the great majority of it.
>
>I agree.

This is everyone's privilege.

>I also feel that the votes so far should be visible to the voters -
>nothing is gained or lost, and I want to know how people who haven't written
>in yet feel. Information wants to be free.

I believe that the votes will be made public when the voting is 
complete.  But I want people to decide on their own, not on the basis of 
what other people have or have not done (which would only encourage the 
factionalism that I am attempting to reduce).

I would in fact be inclined to keep the voting a proper secret ballot, but 
I don't think that yahoogroups polls provide for that.  The virtue of a 
secret ballot should not need to be debated.

